# Vue security

Narrows `core-common-rules`' security rules to Vue render-time and routing
risks. Applies only to `*.vue`; server-side Node.js concerns come from
`ts-js-node`'s security rule.

## Template injection (XSS)

- Never bind `v-html` to user-controlled or unsanitized content. If raw HTML is required, sanitize (e.g. DOMPurify) immediately before the binding and keep the call next to it.
- Prefer `{{ value }}` or `:title="value"` over `v-html` for plain text.
- Allowlist the scheme (`http:`/`https:`/`mailto:`) of a dynamic `:href`/`:src` bound to user-controlled input.
- Never pass a user-controlled string into `h()` as raw HTML, or re-inject raw markup through a hand-built VNode tree.

## Routing and SSR

- Validate and narrow a Vue Router dynamic segment (`route.params.id`) before using it in a query, redirect target, or `v-html`-rendered value.
- In a server-rendered app (Nuxt or custom SSR), never read a secret, session token, or unsanitized request header into a `ref`/`reactive()` value serialized into client-hydrated state.
- Redirect from a navigation guard (`next('/somewhere')`, `router.push()`) to a query-derived target only if it is a same-origin, allowlisted path; never pass a raw `redirect` query value through.

## Store and state exposure

- Do not store a raw auth token or other secret in a Pinia store field covered by a `persist`/localStorage plugin without explicit review.
- Reset (`$reset()` or manual) any Pinia store holding user-specific data on logout.
